  {
    "lesson_id": "052",
    "trigger_word": "pneumonia",
    "trigger_card_number": 851,
    "title": "LESSON 52: BREATH, MUSCLE, BODY",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "PNEUMA (πνεῦμα) is breath, BRONCHOS",
          "(βρόγχος) the windpipe, MYS (μῦς) a",
          "muscle, and SOMA (σῶμα) the body.",
          "",
          "  pneumatic     breath + relating to",
          "  bronchitis    windpipe + inflammation",
          "  myocardium    muscle + heart",
          "  psychosomatic mind + body",
          "",
          "The p of pneuma is silent in English and",
          "sounded in Greek. Every pneumo- word here",
          "keeps the spelling and drops the sound.",
          "",
          "Soma is the body as against the mind, so",
          "a psychosomatic pain is real in the one",
          "and begins in the other.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 19 CARDS: breath, muscle, body."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 52"
      }
    ]
  },
