  {
    "lesson_id": "055",
    "trigger_word": "appendicitis",
    "trigger_card_number": 893,
    "title": "LESSON 55: WHAT THE ENDING SAYS",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "ITIS (-ῖτις) is inflammation, OMA (-ωμα)",
          "a growth, ALGOS (ἄλγος) pain, and ONKOS",
          "(ὄγκος) a mass.",
          "",
          "  meningitis    membrane + inflammation",
          "  melanoma      black + growth",
          "  neuralgia     nerve + pain",
          "  oncology      mass + study",
          "",
          "The ending carries the diagnosis and the",
          "front of the word says where. Any -itis",
          "is inflamed, wherever it sits.",
          "",
          "Glaucoma is the exception. It ends in",
          "-oma and is no growth at all, only the",
          "grey clouding that named it.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 18 CARDS: the endings of illness."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 55"
      }
    ]
  },
