    "trigger_card_number": 911,
    "title": "LESSON 56: WHAT THE SURGEON DOES",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "ECTOMY (ἐκτομή) is a cutting out, OTOMY",
          "(τομή) a cutting into, OSTOMY (στόμα) a",
          "mouth made, PLASTY (πλάσσειν) a moulding,",
          "and SCOPY (σκοπία) a viewing.",
          "",
          "  tonsillectomy  tonsils + taken out",
          "  tracheotomy    windpipe + cut open",
          "  colostomy      colon + new mouth",
          "  rhinoplasty    nose + reshaped",
          "",
          "Three of them differ by one letter and by",
          "the whole operation: ectomy removes the",
          "organ, otomy cuts into it, ostomy leaves",
          "an opening behind.",
          "",
          "Scopy only looks. Nothing is cut.",
          "",
          "THE NEXT 17 CARDS: what surgeons do."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Lesson 56"
      }
    ]
  },
